-- FRESCO-861 (audit-6 A6-L9, derived from FRESCO-819): catalog data that looks wrong in
-- the app, and two checks so it cannot come back.
--
-- 1. Titles and descriptions with a repeated "con" ("Tempeh a la plancha con ajo con
--    limon"), a leftover of how the variants were generated. The second "con" joins
--    the list instead: "con ajo y limon" / "con tamari, jengibre y limon", and an
--    item the title already named is not repeated. 122 names and
--    246 descriptions, each one listed below (id, old text, new text).
--    A description is only touched in its first clause: "ideales para acompañar con
--    arroz" is not a repetition. Slugs stay as they are: they are URLs.
--    Every update fires only while the row still holds the exact old text, so it is
--    idempotent and never overwrites a later edit.
--
-- 2. The category vocabulary of `recipes.clasificacion.categoria`. The code contract
--    (`CategoriaReceta`) listed 12 values while the data held 19. It now lists 18, and
--    the data is brought inside it: `bowl` is the same thing as `bowls`, `vegetal` is
--    `verdura`, and the breakfast recipes tagged `ensalada` whose own name says bowl,
--    porridge, muesli, pudding, batido or yogur move to `bowls`, `batidos` or `lacteos`.
--    The rest of the "category does not fit the meal type" cases (for example sauteed
--    vegetables under `desayuno`) are a different problem, tracked apart.
--
-- 3. `recipes_nombre_sin_con_repetido` and `recipes_categoria_en_contrato`: the database
--    refuses a new recipe name with a repeated "con" and a category outside the contract,
--    whatever wrote the row. Both are added after the data is fixed, in this same
--    transaction: if one row still violates them, nothing is applied.

update public.recipes r
set nombre = v.nuevo
